  "colors": "UR",
  "identity": "A UR graveyard-count control deck. It spends its first five or six turns answering things with the cheapest interaction in the colours, and every one of those answers is simultaneously a card going into its own graveyard -- the attrition IS the win condition's counter. Rise from the Tides then converts the whole yard into a board in a single card: 18 of the 23 nonland cards are instants or sorceries (78.3%), the highest density of any build from this pool, and a turn-7 Rise is realistically 6-9 Zombies for 12-18 power. Seize the Storm reads the same resource as a backup, and Thermo-Alchemist is the one payoff that needs no graveyard at all. Three things to be clear-eyed about: Rise resolves on turn 7 but deals its first damage on turn 8, because the tokens enter tapped AND summoning sick; 6 of the 23 nonland cards carry a flashback the deck must usually DECLINE to cast, because flashback exiles the card out of the very count Rise reads; and random mill is worth only 0.45 of a Zombie per card, so casting cheap spells is the engine and milling is the supplement.",
